// PROMOTED from pending under dense (P8, 2026-08-13): AGREE on the
// dense engines — the class below is resolved by the dense-delivery
// rulings (design/dense_delivery.md); kept as a regression pin.
// The residual leg of frame-state-cross-cycle-jul2026/01: a QUIET POLL
// between two dispatches disarms the interp's framed re-derivation, so a
// later capture fire never re-runs the recursive body.
//
// `GXLambda::update` (graphix-compiler/src/node/lambda.rs) arms the
// framed re-derivation with
//     let framed = self.prev_looped && !event.init
//                  && (entry_fired || externals_triggered(&self.body, event));   (~516)
// and then assigns
//     self.prev_looped = reentered;                                              (~623)
// unconditionally, on EVERY dispatch. `prev_looped` is documented (~487)
// as a statement about BODY STATE — "its innermost frame left the body's
// node state mid-recursion" — but the assignment is unconditional, so a
// dispatch with nothing authoritative to say about that state still
// overwrites it. (Careful, and this matters for the fix: a quiet poll
// DOES run the body — the `if !reentered && !framed { self.body.update(..) }`
// pass executes on every dispatch — it just runs incrementally over the
// leftover state. It can even LOOP, if the tail select re-selects the
// recursive arm, and then the current assignment is correct.)
//
// epoch 0 (defaults): f(1, 0) loops once -> 0. prev_looped = true.
// epoch 1 (in0 = 1): in0 fires, so the enclosing region re-evaluates and
//   f is POLLED — but f's args are constants and its capture in1 did not
//   fire, so nothing triggers it: reentered = false, and prev_looped is
//   silently reset to false. Value 0 + 1 = 1 in both modes.
// epoch 2 (in1 = 2): the capture fires. The kernel's params are formals
//   ++ captures, so the kernel re-derives the whole body and emits
//   acc = in1 = 2, + in0 = 1 -> 3. The interp is not framed (prev_looped
//   was cleared in epoch 1), the retained tail-select arm leaves the
//   recursive arm asleep, and it emits nothing.
//     interp: 0, 1, <nothing>
//     jit:    0, 1, 3
//
// The control proves it is the intervening quiet poll and nothing else —
// drop in0 so no quiet dispatch happens and both modes agree, both fire:
//   // schedule-v1: cap=96 events=768; in1=i64:1; in1=i64:2
//   { let rec f = |n, acc| select n { 0 => acc, _ => f(n - 1, in1) }; f(1, 0) }
//   interp = jit = 0, 1, 2
//
// Fix: leave `prev_looped` alone on a dispatch that is not authoritative
// about it — a pass that ran incrementally over leftover state and did
// not itself loop:
//     if reentered || entry_fired || externals_triggered(..) || event.init {
//         self.prev_looped = reentered;
//     }
// The `reentered` disjunct is load-bearing: a quiet poll that DOES loop
// must still record itself.
//
// Caveat for whoever lands it: this WIDENS the framed population, and
// `framed` is not free — it calls `self.body.reset_replay(ctx)` and runs
// the pass against a private seeded map under a forced init view.
// `reset_replay` discards interior-bottom ride history, which is
// load-bearing for taint-cache-callee-jul2026,
// inloop-bottom-cache-jul2026 and select-merge-taint-ride-aug2026 (a
// `100/x` that bottoms rides its operand cache unframed and bottoms
// framed). It does NOT discard the selection (that is semantic state,
// re-seeded across parks by `SelSnap`), so the strict-select pins should
// hold — but the whole taint-ride corpus plus select-quiet-scrutinee
// must be re-run before this lands.
//
// Direction note: as with tail-zero-iteration-fire-aug2026, the
// NODE-WALK is the side that drops the event here; the kernel matches
// the documented replay-frames v3 rule that a capture fire re-runs the
// body. Worth Eric's confirmation before it lands.
// schedule-v1: cap=96 events=768; in0=i64:1; in1=i64:2
{ let rec f = |n, acc| select n { 0 => acc, _ => f(n - 1, in1) }; f(1, 0) + in0 }
